---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Downloads from '../components/Downloads.astro';
import ContactBand from '../components/ContactBand.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/portrait.webp';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  active="About"
  description="Christopher Flathmann is an Assistant Professor at Clemson, director of BIG CAT, and co-director of Clemson’s Center for Human-AI Interaction, Collaboration, and Teaming."
  dark
>
  <section class="page-hero dark">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
      <h1>
        I lead research on AI
        <br />
        <em>and how people work together.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="page-lead">
        I’m Christopher Flathmann, an Assistant Professor at Clemson University.
        I direct the BIG CAT Research Group and co-direct Clemson’s Center for
        Human-AI Interaction, Collaboration, and Teaming.
      </p>
      <Downloads />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about-body-grid">
      <div>
        <section class="about-section">
          <h2>What I do.</h2>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              I lead research on human–AI teamwork. I set the direction for our
              projects and work with my teams to turn research questions into AI
              systems and studies. I also build systems hands-on.
            </p>
            <p>
              My work connects AI development with the people who have to work
              alongside it. We study how an AI’s behavior changes the team, then
              use what we learn to design AI teammates and train people to work
              with them.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-evidence-links">
            <a class="text-link" href="/work.html">
              Systems and research
              <Arrow />
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="about-section">
          <h2>Some contributions.</h2>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              In my{' '}
              <a href="https://doi.org/10.1145/3637326">
                research on social influence
              </a>
              , people changed their behavior to complement an AI teammate. I
              study that influence because an AI’s place in a team can affect
              how people work with each other, too.
            </p>
            <p>
              With collaborators, I’ve studied{' '}
              <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/0144929X.2024.2396476">
                how AI information-sharing shapes people’s views of their team
              </a>
              . In a survey of hypothetical teams, information about the
              situation and support for team memory most strongly shaped
              participants’ attitudes and how well they thought the team
              understood its work.
            </p>
            <p>
              I also co-authored{' '}
              <a href="/application/Experiment-Design.pdf">
                guidance for designing human–AI teaming experiments
              </a>
              . That work connects the research question with decisions about
              team composition, the environment, and what to measure.
            </p>
            <p>
              I received a 2025 AFOSR Young Investigator Award for research on
              managing conflict in human–AI teams. I also helped start Clemson’s
              Center for Human-AI Interaction, Collaboration, and Teaming, which
              I now co-direct.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
        <section class="about-section">
          <h2>Why I work on this.</h2>
          <div class="prose">
            <p>
              AI should disrupt the processes that need to change. But
              human-human collaboration is getting caught in the crossfire.
            </p>
            <p>
              My research shows how workplace relationships can worsen because
              of AI, knowledge can become harder to manage, and teams can break
              down. Those are problems we have to account for when we build
              these systems.
            </p>
            <p>
              I build AI and train teams to preserve and improve those
              relationships. I want people to be better able to work together
              because the technology is there.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="text-link" href={site.lab}>
            BIG CAT Research Group
            <Arrow diagonal />
          </a>
        </section>
        <section class="about-section">
          <h2>At Clemson.</h2>
          <ul class="appointment-list">
            <li>
              <time>2024–present</time>
              <div>
                <strong>Assistant Professor</strong>
                <span>Human-Centered Computing, School of Computing</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <time>2024–present</time>
              <div>
                <strong>Director, BIG CAT Research Group</strong>
                <span>
                  Building Intelligent Goals for Collaborative AI Technologies
                </span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <time>2024–present</time>
              <div>
                <strong>Co-Director, CU-CHAI</strong>
                <span>
                  Center for Human-AI Interaction, Collaboration, and Teaming
                </span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <time>2023–2024</time>
              <div>
                <strong>Research Assistant Professor</strong>
                <span>Human-Centered Computing</span>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="about-section">
          <h2>Education.</h2>
          <ul class="appointment-list">
            <li>
              <time>2023</time>
              <div>
                <strong>Ph.D., Human-Centered Computing</strong>
                <span>Clemson University · Advisor: Nathan J. McNeese</span>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <time>2018</time>
              <div>
                <strong>B.S., Computer Science</strong>
                <span>Clemson University</span>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>
      <aside class="portrait-wrap">
        <Image
          src={portrait}
          alt="Christopher Flathmann"
          widths={[360, 540, 900]}
          sizes="(max-width: 600px) 90vw, 380px"
          loading="eager"
          class="portrait"
        />
        <span class="portrait-note">Christopher Flathmann · Clemson, SC</span>
        <div class="credential-line">
          <a href="/Resume.pdf">
            Resume <Arrow diagonal />
          </a>
          <a href="/CV.pdf">
            Full academic CV <Arrow diagonal />
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <ContactBand />
</Base>
